# Definition and Need of Venv
# One python app will need a specific version of a module. The other might need another version. 
# Pip installs version of a module globally, affecting all applications
# To provide two versions for two different applicatons, we use Venv

# What is Venv?
# Venv are virtual enviornments
# We use Venv in development, but dont include in git repository or send to github
# in git bash terminal, inside the folder Lesson21
# type py -m venv .venv
# above statement means, creating a virtual enviornment named .venv, which creates a folder! not a file
# type in git bash terminal,  source .venv/Scripts/activate
# (.venv) means its activated
# to deactivate the virtual enviornment, simply in terminal type deactivate
# after the enviornment is activated, you can even get the pip list without py -m pip list preceeding it.
# now we install py -m pip install requests
